---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Notare+ — convenience, never capability"
  description="What Notare+ will charge for (hosted sync, hosted models), what it never will (anything local), and pricing published before launch. Join the waitlist."
>
  <!-- ============ head ============ -->
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">The paid tier, before it exists</p>
      <h1>Notare<span class="plus">+</span> sells convenience.<br />Never capability.</h1>
      <p>
        Most apps announce pricing after you're invested. We're publishing the
        exact boundary between free and paid before Notare+ is even built — so
        you can adopt Notare knowing precisely what the deal is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ what will be paid ============ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">On the meter</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">What Notare+ will charge for</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Exactly one category: things that require us to run servers for you.
        Every one of these has a free local equivalent that keeps working
        whether or not you pay.
      </p>

      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="ledger-row">
          <div>
            <h3>E2E-encrypted cloud sync</h3>
            <span class="tag paid">Paid</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Your Markdown, synced between machines through our relay —
            end-to-end encrypted, so we can't read a word of it. The free
            equivalent: your notes are plain files, sync them with anything
            (Obsidian Sync, Syncthing, git, iCloud).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger-row">
          <div>
            <h3>Hosted transcription</h3>
            <span class="tag paid">Paid</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Server-side STT for when you're on a machine without a GPU, or
            want larger models than your hardware runs comfortably. Local
            Whisper stays free and first-class — hosted is a fallback, not
            the default.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger-row">
          <div>
            <h3>Hosted LLM summaries</h3>
            <span class="tag paid">Paid</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Enhancement on our hosted models, for people who don't want to run
            Ollama or manage API keys. BYO endpoint remains free forever — if
            you have a key or a local model, you never need this.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ledger-row">
          <div>
            <h3>Roaming voice profiles</h3>
            <span class="tag paid">Paid</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Speaker-recognition profiles that follow you across devices, so
            "who said what" is solved on every machine without retraining.
            Per-device profiles stay local and free.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-creed">
        <p class="kicker" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Pricing philosophy</p>
        <p class="big">
          Metered at cost plus a thin margin, with published rates, hard caps,
          and prepaid credits — no surprise bills.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Usage-based, not seat-based: pay for the minutes and tokens you actually use.</li>
          <li>Rates published on this page before launch, and every change announced before it applies.</li>
          <li>Hard caps you set yourself — when credits run out, hosted features pause. Nothing auto-tops-up.</li>
          <li>Prepaid credits, not a subscription treadmill. Unused credits don't expire out from under you.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ what will never be paid ============ -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Never on the meter</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">What will never cost a rupee, dollar, or euro</h2>

      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="ledger-row">
          <div>
            <h3>Everything local</h3>
            <span class="tag free">Free forever</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Recording, local Whisper transcription with GPU acceleration,
            notepad-first AI enhancement via your own LLM, Markdown export to
            any folder, Obsidian vault integration, calendar via your own
            OAuth — the entire app as it exists today, and every local feature
            we ship after this.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="covenant">
        <blockquote>
          Everything that works locally is <strong>free. Forever.</strong>
          No feature you have today will ever move behind a paywall.
          Notare+ will sell convenience — hosted sync and models —
          <strong>never capability.</strong>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="signed">
          — The covenant, verbatim from the homepage. If we ever violate it,
          the code is MIT — fork us and keep everything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ waitlist ============ -->
  <section class="band waitlist" id="waitlist">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Waitlist</p>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="max-width: none;">Be first when Notare+ opens.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        One email when it launches, one when pricing is published. Nothing else.
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: waitlist.notare.dev/subscribe is a placeholder endpoint — wire a
           real handler (Cloudflare Worker + KV, or Buttondown) before launch. -->
      <form method="POST" action="https://waitlist.notare.dev/subscribe">
        <label class="sr-only" for="email" style="position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0);">Email address</label>
        <input
          id="email"
          type="email"
          name="email"
          required
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          autocomplete="email"
        />
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Join the waitlist</button>
      </form>
      <p class="fallback">
        Form not working? Email
        <a href="mailto:plus@notare.dev?subject=Notare%2B%20waitlist">plus@notare.dev</a>
        with the subject "Notare+ waitlist".
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
